  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The deep orange-red colour of cochinita pibil comes from "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "marinating"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "marinating"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the pork in smoked paprika and turmeric, used here as a substitute for traditional achiote paste. Long, slow "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "braising"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "braising"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in citrus juice turns the shoulder into something that shreds with almost no effort. Serve it piled into warm tortillas with pickled onions."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: the longer you marinate, the more vivid the colour. Overnight is ideal but 2 hours still works."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
